        <headline>Flood Warning issued September 25 at 10:43AM CDT until September 26 at 3:00PM CDT by NWS Quad Cities IA IL</headline>
        <description>...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in Iowa...

Wapsipinicon River near De Witt 4S affecting Scott and Clinton
Counties.

Iowa River at Oakville affecting Louisa County.

Iowa River at Wapello affecting Louisa County.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring.

* WHERE...Iowa River at Oakville.

* WHEN...Until Saturday morning.

* IMPACTS...At 12.0 feet, flooding of agricultural land is ongoing.
Several county roads are under water and closed.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 10:00 AM CDT Friday the stage was 12.1 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage
tomorrow morning.
- Flood stage is 11.0 feet.
</description>
        <instruction>

Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars
through flooded areas.

Caution is urged when walking near riverbanks.

The next statement will be issued by Saturday morning.</instruction>
